  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale** hotel project in the Caribbean and Latin America, owners and developers are commonly shortlisting the big global brands with strong regional pipelines, especially **Marriott**, **Hilton**, **Hyatt**, and **IHG**.[3][4][7][17]\n\nThe brands most often associated with this segment in the region include:\n\n- **Marriott International** — especially **JW Marriott**, **The Ritz-Carlton**, **Westin**, and other upscale/luxury flags, with Marriott described as the largest hotel company in the region and a major player in luxury and upscale growth.[4][7][14]\n- **Hilton** — particularly **DoubleTree by Hilton**, **Curio Collection by Hilton**, and **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**, which are highlighted as conversion-friendly or higher-segment brands in the region.[3][17]\n- **Hyatt** — especially **Andaz**, **Thompson**, **Alila**, **Park Hyatt**, and **Hyatt Regency**, with Hyatt’s portfolio in the region spanning from premium to ultra-luxury.[1][13]\n- **IHG Hotels & Resorts** — especially **InterContinental**, **Kimpton**, and **Hotel Indigo**, which are being expanded in Caribbean destinations.[1]\n\nIf the project is specifically a **resort** rather than an urban upper-upscale hotel, the shortlist often leans toward **JW Marriott**, **Hilton Curio/Tapestry**, **Kimpton**, **InterContinental**, **Andaz**, and **Thompson**, because those brands combine strong lifestyle or luxury positioning with regional relevance.[1][4][17]\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into a **developer shortlist by likely asset type** — for example: *urban business hotel, resort, conversion, or mixed-use branded residence*.",
